slides=[]
def s(key,title,subtitle,body='',image=None,section='story',kind='split',points=None):
    slides.append(dict(key=key,title=title,subtitle=subtitle,body=body,image=image,section=section,kind=kind,points=points or []))
s('cover','Stillwater\nGarden.','LANDSCAPES FOR A SLOWER LIFE','A private world of water, wild planting and beautifully quiet architecture. Concept collection / September 2026',image='hero',kind='cover')
s('invitation','Step outside.\nFeel elsewhere.','01 / THE INVITATION','For fictional clients Mira and Sebastiaan de Wilde, the garden becomes the most generous room of the house: a place for long lunches, unhurried walks and the simple pleasure of watching the seasons change.',image='hero',points=['Imagined location: wooded edge of the Dutch Veluwe','Illustrative garden plot: 1,400 m²','Demo 02 / Private residential landscape'])
s('brief','A little untamed.\nEntirely considered.','THE DESIGN BRIEF','A garden with enough structure to feel composed and enough life to surprise you.',points=['A place to gather: dining, cooking and conversation','A place to retreat: water, woodland and a quiet bench','A place to notice: flowers, shadows and seasonal change','A clear investment with traceable supplier packages'],kind='principles')
s('overview','One garden.\nMany small worlds.','THE LANDSCAPE AS A WHOLE','Water is the still centre. A loose ribbon of meadow links a social terrace to a woodland edge, while intimate garden rooms reveal themselves along the way. This aerial view is atmospheric; the masterplan sets out the intended zoning.',image='aerial',kind='hero')
s('story','Stillness, framed by life.','THE CONCEPT','A precise line of water meets loose, generous planting. Dark timber creates shelter. Pale stone catches the light. Copper tones connect seedheads, leaves and objects.',image='woodland',points=['Strong spatial structure','Soft, layered planting','A changing experience through the year'])
s('materials','Elements that age\nwith grace.','02 / MATERIAL MOOD','Pale textured limestone, buff gravel, charred timber, natural oak and weathered metal tones. A restrained family of materials allows planting and reflected light to take the lead.',image='materials',section='moodboards',kind='board')
s('botanical','The garden\nis the artwork.','PLANTING MOOD','Violet spires, soft mauve flowers, white glints and grasses that catch the breeze. The woodland edge becomes a quieter composition of ferns, branching trunks and deep green leaves.',image='botanical',section='moodboards',kind='board')
s('palette','Green, in every register.','COLOUR LANGUAGE','Forest and olive form the foundation. Chalk and copper add warmth. A muted violet note threads through the planting.',section='moodboards',kind='palette')
s('seasons','Designed for\nmore than summer.','FOUR SEASONS / ONE PLACE','Spring blossom. Summer abundance. Autumn copper. Winter silhouette. These generated seasonal studies express the intended atmosphere; they are not records of an established garden.',image='seasons',section='moodboards',kind='board')
s('masterplan','A journey,\nnot just a view.','03 / THE MASTERPLAN','Concept zoning for an assumed 40 × 35 m garden. Arrival, water, meadow, woodland, pavilion, lounge and productive garden form one connected route. Dimensions are illustrative; this is not a measured site drawing.',image='masterplan',section='designs',kind='plan')
s('water','The quiet centre.','THE REFLECTING POOL','A long, dark basin mirrors the sky and draws the eye through the garden. Pale coping makes a calm threshold between water and planting. A decorative water feature, conceived for reflection rather than swimming.',image='hero',section='designs',kind='hero')
s('pavilion','Long lunches.\nLate conversations.','THE DINING PAVILION','Charred timber shelters a generous dining table; a slatted canopy filters the evening sun. The outdoor kitchen shown is an optional €12,800 addition to the €32,000 pavilion package.',image='pavilion',section='designs',kind='hero')
s('meadow','Let the edges\ncome alive.','THE MEADOW WALK','Drifts of airy grasses and violet perennials loosen the geometry. A gently curving path creates changing glimpses of the water and pavilion, with generous planted depth on either side.',image='meadow',section='designs',kind='hero')
s('woodland','A room with\na living ceiling.','THE WOODLAND RETREAT','Stone steps through green texture; a solid oak bench in a pocket of light. This is the quietest part of the garden, composed for a slower pace and the pleasure of small details.',image='woodland',section='designs',kind='hero')
s('lounge','Gather a little closer.','THE SUNKEN LOUNGE','A circular seating court offers a more intimate scale within the garden. Limestone benches and soft cushions sit just below the planted edge. Final levels, drainage and accessible circulation require coordinated technical design.',image='lounge',section='designs',kind='hero')
s('potager','A garden you\ncan bring to the table.','THE PRODUCTIVE GARDEN','Four oak beds, herbs, trained fruit and a working ledge make a small daily ritual. The €6,200 package includes the beds, trellis, starter planting and a simple surface water butt.',image='potager',section='designs',kind='hero')
s('plantingplan','Plant in layers.\nRead it as one.','04 / THE PLANTING STRATEGY','A small family of planting characters creates cohesion: meadow matrix, accent drifts, woodland carpet and structural trees. The schedule is a fictional candidate palette, subject to local soil, light and nursery review.',image='plantingplan',section='planting',kind='plan')
s('plants','Texture before colour.','THE CANDIDATE PALETTE','Plant names describe design intent. Final cultivars, quantities and suitability are decisions for the appointed horticultural team after site assessment.',section='planting',kind='plants')
s('section','A landscape\nwith depth.','SECTION / TERRACE TO WOODLAND','The section studies relationships between the house terrace, reflecting basin, meadow and tree canopy. Levels, depths and construction details are intentionally schematic.',image='section',section='designs',kind='plan')
s('waterstrategy','Make room\nfor the rain.','WATER & SITE STRATEGY','Coordinate drainage before the garden is built. The concept separates the decorative water feature from rainfall management, with planted collection areas and an optional storage package.',image='aerial',section='planting',points=['Confirm soil, infiltration and groundwater conditions','Resolve gradients and discharge routes with specialists','Protect existing tree root zones during works','Optional storage system: + €6,400; off by default'])
s('night','When the garden\nchanges its voice.','05 / AFTER DARK','A warm glow under the pavilion. A quiet rhythm along the path. Water holding the last colour of the sky. The dark edges remain part of the composition.',image='night',section='lighting',kind='hero')
s('lightingplan','Light the moments.\nKeep the mystery.','THE LIGHTING CONCEPT','A scene-based lighting concept for arrival, gathering and a final evening walk. Fixture locations are indicative, not an electrical installation plan.',image='lightingplan',section='lighting',kind='plan')
s('lightscenes','Three ways\nto spend an evening.','LIGHTING SCENES','The €12,400 lighting allowance covers fixtures, installation and commissioning. Aim, timing and ecology constraints are resolved with the appointed specialists.',section='lighting',kind='scenes')
s('investment','Beautifully clear\nfrom the ground up.','06 / THE INVESTMENT','€213,400–€221,400 including an €18,000 client-held contingency. Furniture selection creates the range. Optional kitchen and rainwater storage are excluded; unforeseen ground conditions remain unpriced. All figures are fictional and include assumed VAT.',section='budget',kind='budget')
s('suppliers','Every layer,\naccounted for.','THE SUPPLIER STRUCTURE','Included subquotes explain a package price. Additional options increase the total only when selected. The main landscape contract is €64,000; its stone supply is visible two levels below.',section='budget',kind='hierarchy')
s('options','Choose your\nextra pleasures.','OPTIONS & CHOICES','Base selection €213,400. Premium furniture adds €8,000; outdoor kitchen adds €12,800; rainwater storage adds €6,400. With all choices selected: €240,600, including contingency and excluding unpriced site conditions.',section='budget',kind='options')
s('programme','From first line\nto first evening.','07 / THE PROGRAMME','An indicative 24-week delivery journey, with planting timed to the eventual site and nursery programme. The first year of establishment care follows practical handover.',section='delivery',kind='timeline')
s('care','A garden is\nnever quite finished.','ESTABLISHMENT & CARE','Beauty develops through attention. The €5,200 establishment package allows for eight visits, a seasonal review and a care handover. The final regime follows the actual species and site conditions.',image='meadow',section='delivery',points=['Observe establishment and respond to weather','Review irrigation and water-feature performance','Use seasonal cutbacks to retain chosen structure','Record replacements and refine the planting over time'])
s('scope','Before the\nfirst spade.','DECISIONS & SCOPE','Approve the design direction, commission the survey, review material and planting samples, then decide on the options. Final technical design and site evidence guide the build.',section='delivery',kind='principles',points=['Plans are conceptual, not construction documents','All suppliers, clients, quotations and prices are fictional','Images are generated concepts, not completed-project photos','Survey, permits, engineering and exceptional remediation excluded'])
s('closing','Stay a little longer.','STILLWATER GARDEN / DEMO 02','A landscape for gathering, wandering and doing very little at all. Prepared for the fictional de Wilde family by Stillwater Landscape Studio.',image='night',section='delivery',kind='cover')

